1
00:01:32,920 --> 00:01:35,030
[Forging Justice]

2
00:01:35,200 --> 00:01:37,729
[Episode 17]

3
00:01:42,710 --> 00:01:44,560
It's not that I don't want to help you.

4
00:01:44,560 --> 00:01:46,289
I've talked to Xia Yingjie too.

5
00:01:46,789 --> 00:01:48,240
Public opinion and popular sentiment

6
00:01:48,240 --> 00:01:49,039
can sometimes be decisive

7
00:01:49,039 --> 00:01:49,840
for a verdict.

8
00:01:50,360 --> 00:01:51,039
Exposing Song Xiaoguang

9
00:01:51,039 --> 00:01:52,350
aligns with public opinion.

10
00:01:52,350 --> 00:01:53,479
Overturning Wang Youxi's sentence

11
00:01:53,479 --> 00:01:54,710
and clearing Qian Xingliang's name

12
00:01:54,710 --> 00:01:56,310
run against public opinion.

13
00:01:56,400 --> 00:01:57,070
Didn't you yourself say

14
00:01:57,070 --> 00:01:58,310
that when you prosecuted,

15
00:01:58,310 --> 00:01:59,350
the whole room applauded?

16
00:01:59,350 --> 00:02:00,810
What do you expect me to do?

17
00:02:03,760 --> 00:02:05,560
Does Mr. Yuan think the same way?

18
00:02:05,590 --> 00:02:06,040
Him?

19
00:02:07,840 --> 00:02:09,520
He's nowhere near as shrewd as I am.

20
00:02:09,520 --> 00:02:10,520
He's too bookish.

21
00:02:10,800 --> 00:02:12,680
Deep down, he's still
an idealistic young man.

22
00:02:12,680 --> 00:02:13,080
Let me tell you,

23
00:02:13,080 --> 00:02:14,400
sometimes when I take cases for him,

24
00:02:14,400 --> 00:02:16,060
I'm actually protecting him.

25
00:02:16,910 --> 00:02:18,280
He never used to win lawsuits.

26
00:02:18,280 --> 00:02:19,280
In the past two years,

27
00:02:19,280 --> 00:02:20,150
his win rate has doubled.

28
00:02:20,150 --> 00:02:21,750
Do you think he suddenly got enlightened?

29
00:02:21,750 --> 00:02:22,840
It's all because I've been

30
00:02:22,840 --> 00:02:24,360
secretly looking out for him.

31
00:02:24,360 --> 00:02:24,800
I find cases

32
00:02:24,800 --> 00:02:26,710
that are easy to win
and give them to him.

33
00:02:26,710 --> 00:02:27,950
Bro, you think this is easy for me?

34
00:02:27,950 --> 00:02:28,910
I have to make money,

35
00:02:28,910 --> 00:02:30,440
and I have to keep him happy.

36
00:02:32,430 --> 00:02:33,490
If you're so tired,

37
00:02:34,190 --> 00:02:35,530
why don't you stop working with him?

38
00:02:35,530 --> 00:02:36,190
With your ability,

39
00:02:36,190 --> 00:02:37,140
you could start your own firm

40
00:02:37,140 --> 00:02:38,079
and make just as much money.

41
00:02:38,079 --> 00:02:39,120
I'm a sentimental guy.

42
00:02:39,120 --> 00:02:40,250
That's my only flaw.

43
00:02:43,190 --> 00:02:43,590
Lu.

44
00:02:45,190 --> 00:02:46,400
If you say

45
00:02:47,400 --> 00:02:48,260
you love money,

46
00:02:49,310 --> 00:02:49,960
I agree.

47
00:02:51,310 --> 00:02:52,590
But if you say you only care about money,

48
00:02:52,590 --> 00:02:53,400
I disagree.

49
00:02:54,910 --> 00:02:56,840
A person who only cares about money

50
00:02:57,190 --> 00:02:59,050
wouldn't put stones in his shoes.

51
00:03:01,590 --> 00:03:03,390
Why did she tell you everything?

52
00:03:05,520 --> 00:03:06,280
We all know that you want

53
00:03:06,280 --> 00:03:07,210
to take the case.

54
00:03:09,190 --> 00:03:10,390
I'm going back first.

55
00:03:16,280 --> 00:03:16,970
Mr. Yuan.

56
00:03:17,400 --> 00:03:19,710
You really are my last hope.

57
00:03:20,360 --> 00:03:21,280
I know

58
00:03:21,310 --> 00:03:23,079
this is asking a lot,

59
00:03:24,079 --> 00:03:25,840
but if there were any other way,

60
00:03:25,840 --> 00:03:26,640
I wouldn't...

61
00:03:28,520 --> 00:03:29,030
Lu Zeming

62
00:03:29,030 --> 00:03:30,490
brought up this case to me.

63
00:03:32,120 --> 00:03:33,050
I turned it down.

64
00:03:34,160 --> 00:03:35,000
But I never imagined

65
00:03:35,000 --> 00:03:37,329
he'd put in so much work
behind the scenes,

66
00:03:37,910 --> 00:03:39,510
putting stones in his shoes.

67
00:03:41,560 --> 00:03:43,160
He has gone to great lengths.

68
00:03:43,690 --> 00:03:44,440
Normally,

69
00:03:44,470 --> 00:03:45,560
he doesn't like taking

70
00:03:45,560 --> 00:03:47,020
such unprofitable cases.

71
00:03:48,240 --> 00:03:48,960
Then why...

72
00:03:50,030 --> 00:03:52,160
Why did he go through all this trouble?

73
00:03:53,590 --> 00:03:54,190
Actually,

74
00:03:54,200 --> 00:03:55,400
after doing his research

75
00:03:55,400 --> 00:03:56,520
and analysis,

76
00:03:57,520 --> 00:03:59,750
he felt that the chances
of overturning the case were slim.

77
00:03:59,750 --> 00:04:00,400
So,

78
00:04:01,750 --> 00:04:03,750
he didn't want to waste his efforts.

79
00:04:04,750 --> 00:04:06,150
His judgment is correct.

80
00:04:08,430 --> 00:04:10,030
It is indeed very difficult.

81
00:04:10,470 --> 00:04:11,400
Very difficult.

82
00:04:11,960 --> 00:04:13,220
Extremely difficult.

83
00:04:14,520 --> 00:04:16,120
Would you like some peanuts?

84
00:04:18,920 --> 00:04:19,950
Mr. Yuan, I know

85
00:04:20,880 --> 00:04:21,870
the chances of securing an acquittal

86
00:04:21,870 --> 00:04:22,750
are minimal.

87
00:04:24,120 --> 00:04:26,770
But even a commutation
to suspended death sentence

88
00:04:26,770 --> 00:04:27,530
would be

89
00:04:27,560 --> 00:04:28,960
something we could do...

90
00:04:32,040 --> 00:04:33,240
All right, it's late.

91
00:04:34,430 --> 00:04:36,310
You should head back and get some rest.

92
00:04:36,310 --> 00:04:37,980
Then this case...

93
00:04:38,040 --> 00:04:38,800
Comrade Xia,

94
00:04:39,560 --> 00:04:41,159
I understand the situation,

95
00:04:41,340 --> 00:04:43,470
and I can also understand how you feel.

96
00:04:43,630 --> 00:04:44,270
But

97
00:04:44,830 --> 00:04:46,490
I can't promise you anything.

98
00:04:47,310 --> 00:04:48,120
And tonight,

99
00:04:49,100 --> 00:04:49,830
we never met.

100
00:04:50,630 --> 00:04:51,159
Alright?

101
00:05:06,950 --> 00:05:09,000
Hello, who paged 0487?

102
00:05:10,810 --> 00:05:12,000
A gentleman surnamed Yuan

103
00:05:12,000 --> 00:05:13,020
asked you to buy some beer

104
00:05:13,020 --> 00:05:14,750
and go back to him immediately.

105
00:05:17,920 --> 00:05:18,720
Good heavens.

106
00:05:21,800 --> 00:05:22,270
Boss,

107
00:05:22,500 --> 00:05:24,500
where can I find a store around here?

108
00:05:45,260 --> 00:05:46,330
It's so late.

109
00:05:46,360 --> 00:05:47,420
What's this about?

110
00:05:47,800 --> 00:05:48,930
Did you buy the beer?

111
00:05:49,040 --> 00:05:50,540
I banged on the store door

112
00:05:50,600 --> 00:05:52,000
and paid a fortune for it.

113
00:05:52,720 --> 00:05:54,720
Why do you want to drink at this hour?

114
00:05:54,800 --> 00:05:55,600
I can't sleep.

115
00:05:56,070 --> 00:05:57,200
Why can't you sleep?

116
00:05:58,560 --> 00:05:59,290
I don't know.

117
00:06:00,390 --> 00:06:01,190
I want to chat.

118
00:06:01,950 --> 00:06:02,880
Then let's chat.

119
00:06:09,070 --> 00:06:09,680
Zeming.

120
00:06:11,600 --> 00:06:12,160
That day,

121
00:06:12,960 --> 00:06:14,600
I told you
that I have my own value standards

122
00:06:14,600 --> 00:06:16,360
when taking cases.

123
00:06:17,830 --> 00:06:20,190
I really enjoyed listening.
I learned a lot.

124
00:06:20,190 --> 00:06:20,850
Enjoyed it?

125
00:06:21,750 --> 00:06:22,160
Good.

126
00:06:23,240 --> 00:06:24,040
Then

127
00:06:24,480 --> 00:06:25,870
let's talk

128
00:06:27,120 --> 00:06:28,040
about why we

129
00:06:28,920 --> 00:06:30,320
chose to become lawyers.

130
00:06:34,330 --> 00:06:39,810
[No. 2 Detention Center
of Binjiang City, Dongjiang Province]

131
00:06:38,720 --> 00:06:39,650
Qian Xingliang.

132
00:06:40,190 --> 00:06:41,390
Mr. Yuan Yifang has agreed

133
00:06:41,390 --> 00:06:42,390
to take your case.

134
00:06:42,720 --> 00:06:43,270
From now on,

135
00:06:43,270 --> 00:06:44,360
you need to cheer up

136
00:06:44,750 --> 00:06:45,750
and trust the law.

137
00:06:45,750 --> 00:06:46,720
Leave the rest to us,

138
00:06:46,720 --> 00:06:47,300
okay?

139
00:06:47,740 --> 00:06:48,330
Lawyers,

140
00:06:48,360 --> 00:06:50,270
I really didn't do it.

141
00:06:50,950 --> 00:06:52,010
Why would I kill her

142
00:06:52,560 --> 00:06:53,950
for no reason?

143
00:06:54,600 --> 00:06:55,390
When we parted,

144
00:06:55,390 --> 00:06:56,990
she was still alive and well.

145
00:06:57,170 --> 00:06:58,070
Alright, alright, alright.

146
00:06:58,070 --> 00:06:59,600
We know you didn't do it.

147
00:07:00,950 --> 00:07:01,880
Do you really...

148
00:07:03,870 --> 00:07:04,680
believe me?

149
00:07:08,630 --> 00:07:10,630
It doesn't matter if we believe you.

150
00:07:10,970 --> 00:07:13,100
We need to make the law believe you too.

151
00:07:15,960 --> 00:07:17,460
[Defense Authorization Letter]

152
00:07:39,600 --> 00:07:40,530
Drinking again?

153
00:07:40,600 --> 00:07:41,000
Yeah.

154
00:07:41,620 --> 00:07:43,950
-I'll pour you some water.
-Don't bother.

155
00:07:51,560 --> 00:07:52,560
Take a look first.

156
00:07:52,630 --> 00:07:54,430
I'll pour myself another glass.

157
00:08:05,920 --> 00:08:07,320
Why should I look at this?

158
00:08:07,390 --> 00:08:08,790
Just take a look. No harm.

159
00:08:13,830 --> 00:08:15,800
Journalism and media.

160
00:08:17,000 --> 00:08:18,510
Why would I need to learn about that?

161
00:08:18,510 --> 00:08:19,270
These are study materials

162
00:08:19,270 --> 00:08:20,260
for the grad school entrance exam

163
00:08:20,260 --> 00:08:21,390
in journalism and media from our school.

164
00:08:21,390 --> 00:08:24,190
It took me a while to get them
through connections.

165
00:08:26,830 --> 00:08:29,360
Study materials
for the grad school entrance exam?

166
00:08:29,360 --> 00:08:31,480
Why would I take
the grad school entrance exam?

167
00:08:31,480 --> 00:08:32,320
You've been saying lately

168
00:08:32,320 --> 00:08:33,570
that you're not happy with your job,

169
00:08:33,570 --> 00:08:34,549
and that it's not fulfilling.

170
00:08:34,549 --> 00:08:36,010
So I thought you might want

171
00:08:36,440 --> 00:08:37,240
to look into it

172
00:08:37,870 --> 00:08:39,799
and take the exam just for a change.

173
00:08:42,919 --> 00:08:44,210
Well, I've asked around.

174
00:08:44,210 --> 00:08:45,910
They say
the job prospects in journalism and media

175
00:08:45,910 --> 00:08:47,370
are really good right now.

176
00:08:47,510 --> 00:08:48,910
If you get accepted,

177
00:08:49,600 --> 00:08:50,480
you can stay in Beijing,

178
00:08:50,480 --> 00:08:52,940
where there are
far more job opportunities.

179
00:08:53,080 --> 00:08:55,540
Why would I need
to take the grad school exam?

180
00:08:57,510 --> 00:08:58,510
Here's the thing.

181
00:09:05,510 --> 00:09:07,670
A while back, there was word from Beijing

182
00:09:07,670 --> 00:09:09,510
that the Supreme Court is launching

183
00:09:09,510 --> 00:09:11,090
several special initiatives

184
00:09:11,090 --> 00:09:12,240
and is transferring in judges

185
00:09:12,240 --> 00:09:13,320
with solid theoretical foundations

186
00:09:13,320 --> 00:09:15,980
and rich trial experience
from various places.

187
00:09:16,230 --> 00:09:18,030
I submitted my materials today.

188
00:09:18,510 --> 00:09:20,170
They said I have a good chance.

189
00:09:24,670 --> 00:09:26,670
So you've already made up your mind.

190
00:09:27,200 --> 00:09:28,600
You're going to Beijing,

191
00:09:28,800 --> 00:09:30,000
so you want me to take the exam.

192
00:09:30,000 --> 00:09:31,660
You're just here to inform me.

193
00:09:32,030 --> 00:09:33,290
I'm not informing you.

194
00:09:35,000 --> 00:09:36,130
I want to be with you.

195
00:09:39,510 --> 00:09:42,110
Alright, alright.
Beijing matters a lot to me.

196
00:09:42,740 --> 00:09:43,690
Whether I hope

197
00:09:43,720 --> 00:09:44,960
to change something

198
00:09:45,120 --> 00:09:45,870
or

199
00:09:46,390 --> 00:09:47,790
make some achievements,

200
00:09:48,150 --> 00:09:49,480
it's meaningless here.

201
00:09:51,510 --> 00:09:53,040
I have to go back to Beijing.

202
00:10:03,080 --> 00:10:04,390
Add those points

203
00:10:04,390 --> 00:10:05,480
he just mentioned

204
00:10:05,480 --> 00:10:06,810
to the appeal petition.

205
00:10:06,840 --> 00:10:07,910
Make sure it's submitted to the court

206
00:10:07,910 --> 00:10:09,240
before work ends today.

207
00:10:09,270 --> 00:10:09,750
Okay.

208
00:10:10,150 --> 00:10:11,550
I'll head back to Beijing tomorrow

209
00:10:11,550 --> 00:10:13,000
and wait for the second-instance trial
to begin.

210
00:10:13,000 --> 00:10:14,400
I'll go back with you too.

211
00:10:15,360 --> 00:10:16,160
No, you can't.

212
00:10:16,760 --> 00:10:17,670
You have to stay
in the provincial capital.

213
00:10:17,670 --> 00:10:19,410
You have to keep an eye
on the Provincial High Court.

214
00:10:19,410 --> 00:10:20,320
If they don't schedule the trial,

215
00:10:20,320 --> 00:10:21,790
you let me know immediately.

216
00:10:21,790 --> 00:10:23,150
I'll fly back right away.

217
00:10:23,150 --> 00:10:25,390
Death penalty cases are supposed
to go to trial, aren't they?

218
00:10:25,390 --> 00:10:26,990
It's expressly stipulated.

219
00:10:27,150 --> 00:10:28,600
If everything actually followed the rules,

220
00:10:28,600 --> 00:10:29,660
would we be so busy?

221
00:10:31,270 --> 00:10:33,480
I've got piles of work waiting in Beijing.

222
00:10:33,480 --> 00:10:34,570
That Schnell contract

223
00:10:34,570 --> 00:10:35,840
still hasn't been signed.

224
00:10:35,840 --> 00:10:37,700
That's a lot of money. US dollars.

225
00:10:38,240 --> 00:10:40,100
Then what about everything here?

226
00:10:40,100 --> 00:10:40,720
You can't just

227
00:10:40,720 --> 00:10:41,980
dump everything on me.

228
00:10:42,510 --> 00:10:43,870
And who was it that i-insisted

229
00:10:43,870 --> 00:10:44,800
I take this case?

230
00:10:45,080 --> 00:10:46,120
You yourself!

231
00:10:46,150 --> 00:10:47,410
You wouldn't be able to stand it
if you didn't take it.

232
00:10:47,410 --> 00:10:48,030
At 2 in the morning,

233
00:10:48,030 --> 00:10:48,630
you dragged me out,

234
00:10:48,630 --> 00:10:49,290
rambling on

235
00:10:49,370 --> 00:10:50,210
about the mission of lawyers,

236
00:10:50,210 --> 00:10:52,000
the conscience of legal professionals
and all that.

237
00:10:52,000 --> 00:10:52,860
Who? Who was it?

238
00:10:53,320 --> 00:10:54,120
You!

239
00:10:54,320 --> 00:10:55,380
Let me ask you this.

240
00:10:56,080 --> 00:10:56,880
Then who was it

241
00:10:57,290 --> 00:10:58,720
that sent that Xia whatever

242
00:10:58,720 --> 00:11:00,720
to find me in the middle of the night?

243
00:11:00,840 --> 00:11:01,770
It really wasn't me.

244
00:11:01,770 --> 00:11:02,390
If it wasn't you,

245
00:11:02,390 --> 00:11:04,120
how did she know my room number?

246
00:11:06,080 --> 00:11:06,630
You stay.

247
00:11:07,740 --> 00:11:08,600
Remember this.

248
00:11:08,790 --> 00:11:11,000
If the Provincial High Court
doesn't hold a trial

249
00:11:11,000 --> 00:11:11,840
and only does

250
00:11:11,870 --> 00:11:12,870
a written review,

251
00:11:13,520 --> 00:11:15,120
then we won't have any chance at all

252
00:11:15,120 --> 00:11:16,250
for Qian Xingliang.

253
00:11:17,200 --> 00:11:17,530
Also,

254
00:11:17,730 --> 00:11:18,670
keep track of when Song Xiaoguang's case

255
00:11:18,670 --> 00:11:19,470
goes to trial.

256
00:11:20,910 --> 00:11:21,840
Open the door for me.

257
00:11:21,840 --> 00:11:22,770
It's not locked.

258
00:11:27,790 --> 00:11:29,590
The court is now back in session.

259
00:11:29,600 --> 00:11:32,080
Following supplementary investigation

260
00:11:32,320 --> 00:11:33,630
by the Binjiang People's Procuratorate,

261
00:11:33,630 --> 00:11:34,630
it has been decided

262
00:11:34,630 --> 00:11:36,550
to bring Song Xiaoguang, a key member

263
00:11:36,550 --> 00:11:38,360
of Yao Bo's hooligan gang,

264
00:11:38,750 --> 00:11:39,440
to justice

265
00:11:39,870 --> 00:11:42,270
and try him jointly
with the existing case.

266
00:11:42,560 --> 00:11:43,960
Bring in the defendants.

267
00:12:25,310 --> 00:12:26,910
Why only five years, Mentor?

268
00:12:34,440 --> 00:12:36,500
Let's stick to the facts of this case.

269
00:12:37,840 --> 00:12:39,240
They indeed violated

270
00:12:39,270 --> 00:12:40,150
several women,

271
00:12:40,510 --> 00:12:42,570
but the circumstances of these women

272
00:12:42,630 --> 00:12:43,640
are all different.

273
00:12:43,640 --> 00:12:45,810
Some were involved in prostitution.

274
00:12:46,000 --> 00:12:46,510
Some

275
00:12:47,030 --> 00:12:48,030
were consensual.

276
00:12:48,630 --> 00:12:50,000
Only two cases actually

277
00:12:50,030 --> 00:12:51,030
constitute rape.

278
00:12:51,080 --> 00:12:52,300
And Song Xiaoguang

279
00:12:52,390 --> 00:12:54,440
wasn't personally involved in any of them.

280
00:12:54,440 --> 00:12:55,200
As for

281
00:12:56,550 --> 00:12:57,480
the violent acts

282
00:12:57,630 --> 00:12:58,490
and extortion,

283
00:12:58,840 --> 00:13:00,030
neither led to any deaths.

284
00:13:00,030 --> 00:13:01,150
There were only minor injuries.

285
00:13:01,150 --> 00:13:02,150
A young woman

286
00:13:03,680 --> 00:13:04,790
was driven to suicide by them.

287
00:13:04,790 --> 00:13:05,930
Mentor, if you say that...

288
00:13:05,930 --> 00:13:07,390
Enough, stop right there.

289
00:13:07,640 --> 00:13:08,480
Based on the materials

290
00:13:08,480 --> 00:13:09,510
we have right now,

291
00:13:09,720 --> 00:13:11,780
this matter is really hard to define.

292
00:13:13,680 --> 00:13:14,450
Besides,

293
00:13:14,480 --> 00:13:16,100
Song Xiaoguang's family

294
00:13:16,130 --> 00:13:17,930
has already made generous compensation,

295
00:13:17,930 --> 00:13:18,710
and the victim's family

296
00:13:18,710 --> 00:13:20,600
has expressed their forgiveness.

297
00:13:20,600 --> 00:13:21,930
The Qiao family doesn't lack money at all.

298
00:13:21,930 --> 00:13:23,240
There's no real forgiveness there.

299
00:13:23,240 --> 00:13:25,390
They were definitely pressured into it.

300
00:13:25,390 --> 00:13:25,870
You...

301
00:13:31,270 --> 00:13:32,150
The fact

302
00:13:32,560 --> 00:13:33,910
that we managed to drag Song Xiaoguang

303
00:13:33,910 --> 00:13:35,720
out of the psychiatric hospital

304
00:13:35,910 --> 00:13:37,510
and put him in the defendant's seat

305
00:13:37,510 --> 00:13:39,750
is already a significant victory.

306
00:13:40,480 --> 00:13:41,390
Besides, his father

307
00:13:41,390 --> 00:13:43,670
is currently under investigation
by the Disciplinary Committee.

308
00:13:43,670 --> 00:13:45,510
What more do you want?

309
00:13:47,320 --> 00:13:50,180
I think Song Xiaoguang
deserves the death penalty.

310
00:13:58,030 --> 00:13:59,830
I'm going to the restroom first.

311
00:14:09,550 --> 00:14:10,810
Going to the restroom.

312
00:14:16,390 --> 00:14:18,200
You brought that lawyer
named Yuan Yifang in

313
00:14:18,200 --> 00:14:20,400
through your connections, didn't you?

314
00:14:23,550 --> 00:14:25,390
Enough of this.

315
00:14:26,140 --> 00:14:27,170
We old-timers

316
00:14:27,200 --> 00:14:28,460
can see our younger selves

317
00:14:28,460 --> 00:14:29,650
in you.

318
00:14:30,000 --> 00:14:31,860
Everyone holds you in high regard.

319
00:14:31,860 --> 00:14:33,080
You still have to build your career

320
00:14:33,080 --> 00:14:33,980
in Binjiang, you know.

321
00:14:33,980 --> 00:14:36,110
Where are you going with this, Mentor?

322
00:14:36,440 --> 00:14:38,000
Look at the Wang Youxi case.

323
00:14:38,030 --> 00:14:39,530
He was also prosecuted under hooliganism

324
00:14:39,530 --> 00:14:42,440
and received a far heavier sentence
than this defendant.

325
00:14:42,440 --> 00:14:42,720
Wait.

326
00:14:42,720 --> 00:14:43,750
Are you implying

327
00:14:43,790 --> 00:14:44,670
that he must be sentenced to death?

328
00:14:44,670 --> 00:14:45,950
I'm not saying
we should sentence him to death.

329
00:14:45,950 --> 00:14:47,550
Isn't five years a bit too...

330
00:14:53,760 --> 00:14:54,880
I never comment

331
00:14:54,910 --> 00:14:56,200
on other people's verdicts,

332
00:14:56,200 --> 00:14:57,200
even if I think

333
00:14:57,390 --> 00:14:58,920
the sentence was too heavy.

334
00:15:00,720 --> 00:15:01,600
Do you realize

335
00:15:02,140 --> 00:15:03,470
how much risk everyone in this court,

336
00:15:03,470 --> 00:15:05,130
including Court Pres. Jiang,

337
00:15:05,320 --> 00:15:06,870
is bearing for you?

338
00:15:07,630 --> 00:15:08,670
Don't think

339
00:15:08,670 --> 00:15:09,530
that just because you have a little power,

340
00:15:09,530 --> 00:15:11,260
you can use it however you like.

341
00:15:11,480 --> 00:15:12,910
That's the death penalty!

342
00:15:12,910 --> 00:15:16,310
Do you think that's something
you can just hand down on a whim?

343
00:15:16,960 --> 00:15:18,760
Let me give you a piece of advice.

344
00:15:19,120 --> 00:15:20,180
In our line of work,

345
00:15:20,200 --> 00:15:21,390
whether it's handling cases

346
00:15:21,390 --> 00:15:23,030
or conducting yourself in life,

347
00:15:23,030 --> 00:15:25,090
you always need to leave some leeway.

348
00:15:35,600 --> 00:15:37,330
Now, let's reconcile our views

349
00:15:37,480 --> 00:15:38,810
in the collegial panel.

350
00:15:39,080 --> 00:15:39,610
Ms. Yang,

351
00:15:39,960 --> 00:15:41,160
what's your opinion?

352
00:15:44,000 --> 00:15:45,240
I'll go with whatever you decide.

353
00:15:45,240 --> 00:15:45,630
Yu.

354
00:15:48,840 --> 00:15:49,320
I agree.

355
00:16:18,750 --> 00:16:19,610
Prosecutor Xu.

356
00:16:21,270 --> 00:16:22,190
I'm here to ask

357
00:16:22,750 --> 00:16:24,390
what the decision was on my case.

358
00:16:24,390 --> 00:16:25,150
Are we appealing?

359
00:16:25,150 --> 00:16:26,440
Your job is done.

360
00:16:26,840 --> 00:16:28,040
Leave the rest alone.

361
00:16:28,600 --> 00:16:30,720
I cannot leave it alone, Prosecutor Xu.

362
00:16:30,720 --> 00:16:32,180
That's the case I handled.

363
00:16:35,080 --> 00:16:37,600
The Procuratorial Committee,
after careful deliberation,

364
00:16:37,600 --> 00:16:39,060
has decided not to appeal.

365
00:16:39,120 --> 00:16:39,980
Not appealing?

366
00:16:41,300 --> 00:16:42,510
But the sentence was clearly too harsh!

367
00:16:42,510 --> 00:16:43,070
Chen.

368
00:16:44,480 --> 00:16:46,280
When leaders consider a matter,

369
00:16:46,790 --> 00:16:48,550
they not only consider individual cases,

370
00:16:48,550 --> 00:16:50,610
but also consider the social impact.

371
00:16:50,750 --> 00:16:51,480
In this case,

372
00:16:51,600 --> 00:16:53,800
although the verdict was overly harsh,

373
00:16:53,850 --> 00:16:54,670
the public response

374
00:16:54,670 --> 00:16:56,070
has been quite positive.

375
00:16:56,840 --> 00:16:58,150
The police have reported

376
00:16:58,150 --> 00:16:58,820
that

377
00:16:59,550 --> 00:17:00,840
there have been
fewer street fights and brawls

378
00:17:00,840 --> 00:17:01,440
recently.

379
00:17:02,440 --> 00:17:03,510
If we appeal again,

380
00:17:03,920 --> 00:17:05,069
it's hard to say what kind of reaction

381
00:17:05,069 --> 00:17:06,069
it would trigger.

382
00:17:06,310 --> 00:17:08,750
However, we'll talk

383
00:17:08,750 --> 00:17:09,960
to the appellate court

384
00:17:09,960 --> 00:17:11,240
to see if some room for adjustment

385
00:17:11,240 --> 00:17:12,000
can be found.

386
00:17:12,920 --> 00:17:13,680
What if the appellate court

387
00:17:13,680 --> 00:17:15,410
upholds the original verdict?

388
00:17:15,560 --> 00:17:16,720
They don't deserve to die.

389
00:17:16,720 --> 00:17:17,569
Why didn't you think of that

390
00:17:17,569 --> 00:17:19,099
when you were prosecuting?

391
00:17:22,960 --> 00:17:23,400
Chen,

392
00:17:24,420 --> 00:17:26,180
you're a prosecutor, you know.

393
00:17:57,510 --> 00:17:59,170
This is a long-distance call!

394
00:18:09,830 --> 00:18:10,760
Hello, Mr. Yuan.

395
00:18:10,880 --> 00:18:12,310
The Provincial High Court
has decided not to hold a trial.

396
00:18:12,310 --> 00:18:14,510
They will conduct written review only.

397
00:18:14,790 --> 00:18:16,450
I knew they would do this!

398
00:18:16,790 --> 00:18:17,550
Stay there!

399
00:18:17,830 --> 00:18:20,290
I'll fly over
first thing tomorrow morning!

400
00:18:29,830 --> 00:18:30,270
Hello.

401
00:18:32,200 --> 00:18:33,000
Yizhong.

402
00:18:34,710 --> 00:18:35,650
Who? Yizhong?

403
00:18:35,720 --> 00:18:36,450
Give it to me.

404
00:18:37,510 --> 00:18:38,720
Can't I say a few words

405
00:18:38,720 --> 00:18:39,530
to my son?

406
00:18:39,690 --> 00:18:40,000
Come on.

407
00:18:40,000 --> 00:18:41,070
Calling so late must mean

408
00:18:41,070 --> 00:18:42,090
he has something urgent for me.

409
00:18:42,090 --> 00:18:43,290
Fine, fine. You talk.

410
00:18:44,200 --> 00:18:44,880
Geez.

411
00:18:45,880 --> 00:18:46,510
Yizhong,

412
00:18:46,920 --> 00:18:48,270
is your case...

413
00:18:48,720 --> 00:18:49,980
I want to talk to my mom.

414
00:18:54,030 --> 00:18:54,960
W-Wait a moment.

415
00:18:55,920 --> 00:18:56,650
It's for you.

416
00:19:01,240 --> 00:19:01,790
Yizhong,

417
00:19:02,670 --> 00:19:03,750
if you don't have anything pressing,

418
00:19:03,750 --> 00:19:04,880
you can chat with me.

419
00:19:05,520 --> 00:19:06,170
But

420
00:19:06,200 --> 00:19:07,680
if you've got something
to ask your father,

421
00:19:07,680 --> 00:19:08,650
just tell him.

422
00:19:09,110 --> 00:19:10,770
He has been worried about you.

423
00:19:11,070 --> 00:19:11,870
I...

424
00:19:15,030 --> 00:19:16,680
I'll go back to Beijing in a few days

425
00:19:16,680 --> 00:19:17,540
to see you both.

426
00:19:21,270 --> 00:19:21,830
Okay.

427
00:19:22,960 --> 00:19:23,830
When you come back,

428
00:19:23,830 --> 00:19:25,830
I'll make you something delicious.

429
00:19:27,000 --> 00:19:27,660
That's all.

430
00:19:49,480 --> 00:19:49,880
Hello.

431
00:19:50,270 --> 00:19:50,800
Yizhong.

432
00:19:51,640 --> 00:19:52,440
I've said it before.

433
00:19:52,440 --> 00:19:53,640
As a legal professional

434
00:19:53,640 --> 00:19:54,820
and a prosecutor,

435
00:19:55,030 --> 00:19:56,660
projecting all your energy and anger

436
00:19:56,660 --> 00:19:57,610
onto

437
00:19:57,640 --> 00:19:58,830
a specific case

438
00:19:59,160 --> 00:20:00,220
is not a good thing.

439
00:20:00,480 --> 00:20:01,350
When we discuss

440
00:20:01,370 --> 00:20:02,890
a legal issue,

441
00:20:02,920 --> 00:20:03,310
it...

442
00:20:05,160 --> 00:20:06,720
w-we need to have a...

443
00:20:08,750 --> 00:20:09,480
relatively...

444
00:20:09,480 --> 00:20:10,540
How should I put it?

445
00:20:11,100 --> 00:20:12,500
W-We need to be rational.

446
00:20:12,610 --> 00:20:14,060
As your father,

447
00:20:14,270 --> 00:20:16,640
I completely trust

448
00:20:16,790 --> 00:20:18,270
any decision you make.

449
00:20:19,350 --> 00:20:20,410
I just hope

450
00:20:20,440 --> 00:20:22,240
when we discuss issues,

451
00:20:22,260 --> 00:20:23,260
we can do it in a way

452
00:20:23,790 --> 00:20:24,720
that is rational

453
00:20:24,720 --> 00:20:27,440
and as thorough and careful as possible.

454
00:20:28,880 --> 00:20:29,610
Don't worry.

455
00:20:29,830 --> 00:20:31,030
I won't say things like

456
00:20:31,030 --> 00:20:32,000
"wait a little longer,"

457
00:20:32,000 --> 00:20:33,070
"have patience,"

458
00:20:33,590 --> 00:20:35,450
or "don't be spineless" anymore.

459
00:20:36,680 --> 00:20:37,480
Your life

460
00:20:37,920 --> 00:20:39,110
is yours to live.

461
00:20:39,720 --> 00:20:40,110
I just...

462
00:20:40,110 --> 00:20:40,510
Dad.

463
00:20:42,720 --> 00:20:44,320
I might have killed someone.

464
00:20:46,750 --> 00:20:48,440
W-What? What did you say?

465
00:20:49,640 --> 00:20:50,440
What's wrong?

466
00:21:14,070 --> 00:21:14,550
Resign?

467
00:21:15,680 --> 00:21:17,140
Just because of this case?

468
00:21:18,030 --> 00:21:18,510
Yes.

469
00:21:21,980 --> 00:21:23,750
To be honest, this case

470
00:21:25,310 --> 00:21:26,590
hit me hard.

471
00:21:28,440 --> 00:21:29,270
But it also made me realize

472
00:21:29,270 --> 00:21:30,930
where my problem really lies.

473
00:21:33,550 --> 00:21:35,070
I feel there's still a gap

474
00:21:35,480 --> 00:21:36,270
between me

475
00:21:36,800 --> 00:21:38,170
and a mature, qualified

476
00:21:38,200 --> 00:21:39,400
legal professional.

477
00:21:41,440 --> 00:21:42,500
I should go back to school

478
00:21:42,500 --> 00:21:43,760
to further my studies.

479
00:21:47,080 --> 00:21:48,790
I've been a prosecutor for so many years,

480
00:21:48,790 --> 00:21:50,390
and I've found that everyone

481
00:21:50,720 --> 00:21:51,790
complains that the sword of justice

482
00:21:51,790 --> 00:21:52,920
isn't sharp enough.

483
00:21:53,790 --> 00:21:55,070
But very few realize

484
00:21:55,510 --> 00:21:57,110
that if you can't sheathe it,

485
00:21:57,160 --> 00:21:57,960
waving it around carelessly

486
00:21:57,960 --> 00:21:59,620
can easily hurt the innocent.

487
00:22:00,310 --> 00:22:01,200
Of course, I'm not saying

488
00:22:01,200 --> 00:22:03,020
that Wang Youxi and his wife are innocent.

489
00:22:03,020 --> 00:22:03,880
I've always believed

490
00:22:03,880 --> 00:22:05,750
that a prosecutor shouldn't be too young.

491
00:22:05,750 --> 00:22:06,350
Because in this line of work,

492
00:22:06,350 --> 00:22:08,280
you can't do without common sense.

493
00:22:09,410 --> 00:22:10,070
Your theoretical knowledge

494
00:22:10,070 --> 00:22:10,880
is solid.

495
00:22:10,900 --> 00:22:12,050
What you lack is

496
00:22:12,880 --> 00:22:14,020
an understanding of society

497
00:22:14,020 --> 00:22:15,500
and human relationships.

498
00:22:16,790 --> 00:22:18,790
You need more experience out there.

499
00:22:22,000 --> 00:22:23,480
Mentor, you mean...

500
00:22:24,610 --> 00:22:25,680
Yizhong, let me be straight with you.

501
00:22:25,680 --> 00:22:27,540
Y-You carry too much on your mind.

502
00:22:28,220 --> 00:22:29,400
Sometimes you're too emotional

503
00:22:29,400 --> 00:22:30,530
and too idealistic.

504
00:22:30,930 --> 00:22:32,110
You just mentioned going back to school,

505
00:22:32,110 --> 00:22:32,750
and I think

506
00:22:33,830 --> 00:22:35,290
it's a pretty good choice.

507
00:22:46,220 --> 00:22:47,390
[The High People's Court
of Dongjiang Province]

508
00:22:46,270 --> 00:22:47,400
I couldn't stop him.

509
00:22:47,440 --> 00:22:49,240
He's come several times already.

510
00:22:49,240 --> 00:22:50,440
I've told him.

511
00:22:50,750 --> 00:22:51,830
Mr. Yuan, I'm negotiating here.

512
00:22:51,830 --> 00:22:53,230
He's still waiting here.

513
00:22:54,750 --> 00:22:56,070
I... Well, I...

514
00:22:56,560 --> 00:22:57,200
Hey, what's your surname?

515
00:22:57,200 --> 00:22:57,570
You...

516
00:22:57,570 --> 00:22:58,680
This is Yuan Yifang.

517
00:22:58,680 --> 00:22:59,210
Y-You...

518
00:22:59,320 --> 00:23:00,640
How could you snatch the phone?

519
00:23:00,640 --> 00:23:01,970
Where are your manners?

520
00:23:02,800 --> 00:23:03,550
I am the defense lawyer

521
00:23:03,550 --> 00:23:05,080
for the appellant, Qian Xingliang.

522
00:23:05,080 --> 00:23:06,440
Hello, this is Yuan Yifang.

523
00:23:06,440 --> 00:23:06,840
You...

524
00:23:07,520 --> 00:23:08,440
He's always had a short temper.

525
00:23:08,440 --> 00:23:09,510
He acts like this with everyone.

526
00:23:09,510 --> 00:23:10,700
Doesn't he have any manners at all?

527
00:23:10,700 --> 00:23:11,730
I'm really sorry.

528
00:23:12,030 --> 00:23:13,290
Sorry for the trouble.

529
00:23:13,480 --> 00:23:14,410
What do you mean?

530
00:23:30,000 --> 00:23:31,030
Sorry, you two.

531
00:23:31,440 --> 00:23:32,350
Sorry to keep you waiting.

532
00:23:32,350 --> 00:23:33,350
Presiding Judge.

533
00:23:33,510 --> 00:23:34,040
Mr. Yuan.

534
00:23:35,070 --> 00:23:36,130
My surname is Qiao.

535
00:23:36,200 --> 00:23:38,460
In fact, I was once your student of sorts.

536
00:23:39,590 --> 00:23:41,190
Back when you were teaching,

537
00:23:41,350 --> 00:23:43,350
I had the privilege
of auditing your classes.

538
00:23:43,350 --> 00:23:44,440
Presiding Judge Qiao.

539
00:23:44,440 --> 00:23:46,070
Forgive me for speaking plainly.

540
00:23:46,070 --> 00:23:48,070
Why is such a major
death penalty appeal case

541
00:23:48,070 --> 00:23:49,870
not scheduled for an open trial?

542
00:23:53,000 --> 00:23:54,000
You two, please sit down first.

543
00:23:54,000 --> 00:23:55,040
Have a seat.

544
00:23:55,070 --> 00:23:56,090
I'll explain it slowly.

545
00:23:56,090 --> 00:23:57,440
I'll stand and listen.

546
00:23:57,480 --> 00:23:58,740
I'll stand and listen.

547
00:24:02,440 --> 00:24:03,700
Here's the situation.

548
00:24:04,590 --> 00:24:05,590
First,

549
00:24:05,910 --> 00:24:07,830
we've had too many cases piled up lately.

550
00:24:07,830 --> 00:24:09,090
We're really swamped.

551
00:24:10,110 --> 00:24:11,070
Second,

552
00:24:12,200 --> 00:24:13,200
we've actually already

553
00:24:13,200 --> 00:24:14,330
reviewed this case.

554
00:24:14,680 --> 00:24:16,210
The facts are fairly clear,

555
00:24:16,230 --> 00:24:17,510
and the evidence is quite solid.

556
00:24:17,510 --> 00:24:18,970
You haven't even held a trial yet.

557
00:24:18,970 --> 00:24:19,590
You haven't even

558
00:24:19,590 --> 00:24:20,290
heard our arguments.

559
00:24:20,290 --> 00:24:21,350
And you're so sure?

560
00:24:21,930 --> 00:24:23,240
But you have already submitted

561
00:24:23,240 --> 00:24:24,180
your defense arguments.

562
00:24:24,180 --> 00:24:25,910
The whole point of an open trial

563
00:24:26,070 --> 00:24:27,400
is to present evidence publicly,

564
00:24:27,400 --> 00:24:28,160
conduct cross-examination,

565
00:24:28,160 --> 00:24:31,000
distinguish right from wrong
and ascertain the truth.

566
00:24:31,000 --> 00:24:32,000
Isn't that right?

567
00:24:32,240 --> 00:24:34,160
If you only need
to read the defense arguments,

568
00:24:34,160 --> 00:24:34,960
then I suppose

569
00:24:35,150 --> 00:24:38,080
the first-instance trial
wasn't necessary either?

570
00:24:39,830 --> 00:24:40,360
Mr. Yuan.

571
00:24:41,270 --> 00:24:42,470
Let me put it this way.

572
00:24:43,200 --> 00:24:44,930
This is a collective decision.

573
00:24:45,440 --> 00:24:46,270
How about this?

574
00:24:46,270 --> 00:24:47,830
I'll take your opinions back,

575
00:24:47,830 --> 00:24:48,160
okay?

576
00:24:49,510 --> 00:24:49,960
Okay.

577
00:24:50,590 --> 00:24:51,190
Thank you.

578
00:24:51,550 --> 00:24:54,210
Then you might as well
take a few more words back.

579
00:24:55,000 --> 00:24:56,070
We believe there are many doubts

580
00:24:56,070 --> 00:24:57,000
about this case,

581
00:24:57,960 --> 00:25:00,440
and the first-instance verdict
is highly problematic.

582
00:25:00,440 --> 00:25:01,030
If the second-instance trial

583
00:25:01,030 --> 00:25:02,160
is not held in open court,

584
00:25:02,160 --> 00:25:04,090
we will appeal to the Supreme Court

585
00:25:04,200 --> 00:25:05,260
and make it public.

586
00:25:05,790 --> 00:25:07,050
Presiding Judge Qiao.

587
00:25:07,110 --> 00:25:07,960
We're not just speaking

588
00:25:07,960 --> 00:25:09,960
for the appellant, Qian Xingliang.

589
00:25:10,000 --> 00:25:12,160
We're also speaking for the law itself.

590
00:25:12,160 --> 00:25:14,640
We hope you will give this
your serious consideration.

591
00:25:14,640 --> 00:25:15,640
Mr. Yuan...

592
00:25:21,440 --> 00:25:22,070
Mr. Yuan.

593
00:25:23,070 --> 00:25:24,750
I will definitely convey your message

594
00:25:24,750 --> 00:25:27,050
and actively push for an open trial.

595
00:25:29,270 --> 00:25:29,640
Okay.

596
00:25:32,790 --> 00:25:33,720
Look, everyone.

597
00:25:34,080 --> 00:25:36,000
The distance from Xiashui Village,
where the appellant lives,

598
00:25:36,000 --> 00:25:37,050
to the primary crime scene

599
00:25:37,050 --> 00:25:38,000
is less than 3 kilometers,

600
00:25:38,000 --> 00:25:39,400
but there is a river in between.

601
00:25:39,400 --> 00:25:40,490
Neither the appellant, Qian Xingliang,

602
00:25:40,490 --> 00:25:41,440
nor the victim, Yu Sanhua,

603
00:25:41,440 --> 00:25:42,110
can swim.

604
00:25:42,510 --> 00:25:44,200
For them to get from Xiashui Village

605
00:25:44,200 --> 00:25:45,330
to the murder scene,

606
00:25:45,880 --> 00:25:46,510
they would

607
00:25:47,170 --> 00:25:47,930
have to go

608
00:25:47,960 --> 00:25:49,890
around a pontoon bridge
more than 5 kilometers away,

609
00:25:49,890 --> 00:25:51,350
and then double back about 3 kilometers

610
00:25:51,350 --> 00:25:52,590
to reach the grove.

611
00:25:54,720 --> 00:25:56,780
We checked meteorological records.

612
00:25:57,200 --> 00:25:58,030
During the week of the incident,

613
00:25:58,030 --> 00:25:58,800
temperatures remained high,

614
00:25:58,800 --> 00:26:00,170
ranging from 35

615
00:26:00,200 --> 00:26:01,460
to 37 degrees Celsius,

616
00:26:01,640 --> 00:26:02,350
with humidity

617
00:26:02,350 --> 00:26:03,400
above 60%.

618
00:26:03,720 --> 00:26:06,000
It was hot and stuffy,
like a giant steam room.

619
00:26:06,000 --> 00:26:07,060
No one could endure

620
00:26:07,070 --> 00:26:08,270
such weather easily.

621
00:26:08,720 --> 00:26:10,250
So what I want to ask is this.

622
00:26:10,490 --> 00:26:11,960
What possible reason could Yu Sanhua,

623
00:26:11,960 --> 00:26:14,320
who had discussed divorce
with the appellant

624
00:26:14,320 --> 00:26:15,480
and had a big fight with him,

625
00:26:15,480 --> 00:26:17,500
have had
to willingly endure the scorching heat

626
00:26:17,500 --> 00:26:18,350
and walk such a long distance

627
00:26:18,350 --> 00:26:19,480
with the appellant?

628
00:26:20,160 --> 00:26:21,740
According
to the first-instance prosecutor,

629
00:26:21,740 --> 00:26:22,640
Qian Xingliang even

630
00:26:22,640 --> 00:26:24,770
brought a kitchen knife as his weapon.

631
00:26:24,970 --> 00:26:26,690
But throughout that summer,

632
00:26:26,720 --> 00:26:29,070
Qian Xingliang's usual attire

633
00:26:29,200 --> 00:26:31,600
was ordinary pants
and a blue dacron shirt.

634
00:26:31,650 --> 00:26:33,890
Where could he have hidden
this wide-backed cleaver

635
00:26:33,890 --> 00:26:35,650
that is 320 millimetres long

636
00:26:35,680 --> 00:26:37,140
and weighs over 400 grams?

637
00:26:39,040 --> 00:26:40,070
And what about the 3 urea bags

638
00:26:40,070 --> 00:26:41,920
he prepared for disposing of the body?

639
00:26:41,920 --> 00:26:43,310
Did he just carry them openly?

640
00:26:43,310 --> 00:26:44,310
Isn't it strange?

641
00:26:44,720 --> 00:26:46,960
Isn't it suspicious? Isn't it ridiculous?

642
00:26:46,960 --> 00:26:48,020
Wouldn't Yu Sanhua

643
00:26:48,110 --> 00:26:49,400
have sensed something was off?

644
00:26:49,400 --> 00:26:51,030
Wouldn't she have sensed the danger?

645
00:26:51,030 --> 00:26:51,900
Nonsense!

646
00:26:52,110 --> 00:26:53,750
You've taken dirty money!

647
00:26:54,070 --> 00:26:55,730
My daughter was killed by him!

648
00:26:55,790 --> 00:26:56,400
Gallery!

649
00:26:57,030 --> 00:26:58,090
Mom, stop talking.

650
00:26:58,270 --> 00:26:59,330
Order in the court.

651
00:27:02,480 --> 00:27:03,080
Continue.

652
00:27:03,720 --> 00:27:04,070
Okay.

653
00:27:05,310 --> 00:27:08,110
Even if we assume
Qian Xingliang talked Yu Sanhua into it

654
00:27:08,110 --> 00:27:09,370
with his smooth tongue

655
00:27:09,960 --> 00:27:11,350
and hid the knife

656
00:27:11,510 --> 00:27:12,840
and the bags perfectly,

657
00:27:13,030 --> 00:27:14,630
let's do the math on the time.

658
00:27:15,640 --> 00:27:16,570
In mid-October,

659
00:27:17,310 --> 00:27:18,640
with a cool breeze blowing,

660
00:27:18,640 --> 00:27:20,750
I, a healthy man,

661
00:27:21,030 --> 00:27:22,880
walked 16 kilometers at a fast pace,

662
00:27:22,880 --> 00:27:24,510
without stopping
and without committing any crime,

663
00:27:24,510 --> 00:27:26,280
and it took me
three and a half hours total.

664
00:27:26,280 --> 00:27:26,950
Keep in mind

665
00:27:27,690 --> 00:27:29,240
that I'm talking about ideal weather

666
00:27:29,240 --> 00:27:30,500
and ideal conditions.

667
00:27:30,500 --> 00:27:32,370
And on that day, Yu Sanhua

668
00:27:32,400 --> 00:27:33,830
was wearing mid-heel leather sandals.

669
00:27:33,830 --> 00:27:34,890
When we add the time

670
00:27:35,030 --> 00:27:37,160
needed for the murder,
dismemberment

671
00:27:37,350 --> 00:27:38,410
and body disposal,

672
00:27:38,500 --> 00:27:39,440
a reasonable estimate

673
00:27:39,440 --> 00:27:40,920
puts the minimum required time
at 5.5 hours.

674
00:27:40,920 --> 00:27:41,720
Furthermore,

675
00:27:42,000 --> 00:27:42,930
we have evidence

676
00:27:43,640 --> 00:27:45,400
that around the time of the incident,
Qian Xingliang

677
00:27:45,400 --> 00:27:47,590
developed an infection
from cutting corns

678
00:27:47,590 --> 00:27:48,320
off his foot,

679
00:27:48,440 --> 00:27:49,920
which made it difficult for him to walk.

680
00:27:49,920 --> 00:27:51,200
Let me explain to everyone

681
00:27:51,200 --> 00:27:52,000
what a corn is.

682
00:27:52,030 --> 00:27:53,880
A corn is a...

683
00:27:53,900 --> 00:27:54,900
Defense counsel,

684
00:27:55,160 --> 00:27:57,310
refrain from lengthy
explanatory digressions.

685
00:27:57,310 --> 00:27:58,710
Stick to your key points.

686
00:27:58,880 --> 00:28:00,020
Yes, Presiding Judge.

687
00:28:00,020 --> 00:28:00,560
The key point is

688
00:28:00,560 --> 00:28:01,480
that I recreated the entire route

689
00:28:01,480 --> 00:28:02,510
at the walking pace

690
00:28:02,510 --> 00:28:03,790
of someone in his condition,

691
00:28:03,790 --> 00:28:05,170
and with the time needed for the crime
added in,

692
00:28:05,170 --> 00:28:06,310
the whole process would take

693
00:28:06,310 --> 00:28:08,040
a total of nine and a half hours!

694
00:28:16,440 --> 00:28:17,370
We have witnesses confirming

695
00:28:17,370 --> 00:28:19,400
that Yu Sanhua entered Xiashui Village

696
00:28:19,400 --> 00:28:20,350
around 2 in the afternoon.

697
00:28:20,350 --> 00:28:21,350
Even if she had left immediately

698
00:28:21,350 --> 00:28:23,000
with Qian Xingliang
without a moment's pause,

699
00:28:23,000 --> 00:28:24,510
by the time Qian Xingliang
finished everything

700
00:28:24,510 --> 00:28:25,880
and limped back to the village

701
00:28:25,880 --> 00:28:26,540
in the dark,

702
00:28:26,680 --> 00:28:29,280
it would have been
at least 11 o'clock at night.

703
00:28:29,510 --> 00:28:30,920
However, multiple witnesses have confirmed

704
00:28:30,920 --> 00:28:32,280
that during the days of the incident,

705
00:28:32,280 --> 00:28:33,680
Qian Xingliang was playing cards
at the village entrance

706
00:28:33,680 --> 00:28:35,330
around 6 or 7 in the evening.

707
00:28:35,410 --> 00:28:36,200
He simply didn't have

708
00:28:36,200 --> 00:28:37,800
the time to commit the crime!

709
00:28:45,030 --> 00:28:45,630
Moreover,

710
00:28:46,270 --> 00:28:47,730
there are inherent doubts

711
00:28:48,030 --> 00:28:49,550
regarding the victim's identification!

712
00:28:49,550 --> 00:28:50,880
He's talking nonsense!

713
00:28:51,350 --> 00:28:54,010
He's talking nonsense!
He's talking nonsense!

714
00:28:54,400 --> 00:28:55,410
Judges,

715
00:28:55,440 --> 00:28:56,980
you can't listen to his nonsense!

716
00:28:56,980 --> 00:28:57,510
Bailiff,

717
00:28:57,880 --> 00:29:00,480
remove the family members
from the courtroom.

718
00:29:01,340 --> 00:29:01,900
You...

719
00:29:02,440 --> 00:29:03,510
Officers,

720
00:29:04,210 --> 00:29:04,810
please...

721
00:29:05,310 --> 00:29:06,460
please try to understand

722
00:29:06,460 --> 00:29:07,860
the feelings of a mother!

723
00:29:08,830 --> 00:29:09,680
Presiding Judge!

724
00:29:09,680 --> 00:29:10,680
Presiding Judge!

725
00:29:10,680 --> 00:29:11,740
We will stay quiet.

726
00:29:11,750 --> 00:29:13,510
We trust in the fairness of the law.

727
00:29:13,510 --> 00:29:14,040
I promise

728
00:29:14,290 --> 00:29:15,350
we will stay quiet.

729
00:29:15,480 --> 00:29:16,200
We'll stay quiet.

730
00:29:16,200 --> 00:29:17,200
We'll stay quiet.

731
00:29:20,310 --> 00:29:22,310
Defense counsel, please continue.

732
00:29:29,000 --> 00:29:30,530
Honorable Presiding Judge

733
00:29:30,920 --> 00:29:31,580
and Judges,

734
00:29:31,830 --> 00:29:33,050
today we are here

735
00:29:33,510 --> 00:29:35,640
to hear a murder case.

736
00:29:36,510 --> 00:29:38,840
The appellant has already been sentenced

737
00:29:39,030 --> 00:29:40,760
to death in the first instance.

738
00:29:41,550 --> 00:29:42,270
It is fair to say

739
00:29:42,270 --> 00:29:43,440
that his life now

740
00:29:44,070 --> 00:29:46,800
rests in the hands of the three of you
on the bench.

741
00:29:54,030 --> 00:29:55,090
The death penalty,

742
00:29:55,970 --> 00:29:56,920
as the harshest punishment

743
00:29:56,920 --> 00:29:58,110
in criminal law,

744
00:29:59,110 --> 00:30:00,770
ends a person's life directly

745
00:30:00,880 --> 00:30:02,210
in the name of the state.

746
00:30:03,010 --> 00:30:04,240
Therefore, we must exercise

747
00:30:04,240 --> 00:30:05,640
the utmost caution.

748
00:30:06,880 --> 00:30:08,210
In death penalty cases,

749
00:30:09,030 --> 00:30:10,290
we cannot be satisfied

750
00:30:10,550 --> 00:30:12,160
with basically clear facts

751
00:30:13,440 --> 00:30:15,500
and basically conclusive evidence.

752
00:30:15,680 --> 00:30:17,010
Instead, we must ensure

753
00:30:17,310 --> 00:30:19,040
that the facts are truly clear,

754
00:30:20,350 --> 00:30:22,680
that the evidence is truly sufficient,

755
00:30:23,720 --> 00:30:24,680
and that all reasonable doubts

756
00:30:24,680 --> 00:30:25,810
have been excluded.

757
00:30:28,640 --> 00:30:29,270
Then has this case

758
00:30:29,270 --> 00:30:30,400
met that standard?

759
00:30:32,960 --> 00:30:33,760
Everyone here

760
00:30:34,030 --> 00:30:36,230
is an experienced legal professional.

761
00:30:37,840 --> 00:30:39,110
If we sentence the appellant to death

762
00:30:39,110 --> 00:30:40,640
when the facts and evidence

763
00:30:41,480 --> 00:30:43,350
are unclear,

764
00:30:45,160 --> 00:30:46,960
how will we live with ourselves?

765
00:30:47,920 --> 00:30:49,680
And how can we face

766
00:30:49,880 --> 00:30:52,010
the national emblem hanging above us?

767
00:30:57,600 --> 00:30:58,280
You two,

768
00:30:58,310 --> 00:30:59,310
share your views.

769
00:31:01,440 --> 00:31:02,790
There are some problems with the evidence.

770
00:31:02,790 --> 00:31:03,960
The new evidence
submitted by the defense counsel today

771
00:31:03,960 --> 00:31:05,400
is also very compelling.

772
00:31:05,790 --> 00:31:07,400
If we go by the diagram,

773
00:31:07,700 --> 00:31:09,370
Qian Xingliang couldn't

774
00:31:09,400 --> 00:31:10,400
have completed the crime.

775
00:31:10,400 --> 00:31:12,420
Is it possible that he hitched a ride?

776
00:31:12,420 --> 00:31:13,160
What if he drove

777
00:31:13,160 --> 00:31:14,690
a walking tractor himself?

778
00:31:14,970 --> 00:31:15,590
Or he rode a bicycle

779
00:31:15,590 --> 00:31:16,510
with Yu Sanhua?

780
00:31:17,510 --> 00:31:19,270
If he had any
of these means of transport,

781
00:31:19,270 --> 00:31:20,070
the questions

782
00:31:20,270 --> 00:31:21,070
about the cleaver,
the 3 urea sacks,

783
00:31:21,070 --> 00:31:22,790
and most crucially the timeline,

784
00:31:22,790 --> 00:31:24,720
could all be reasonably explained.

785
00:31:24,720 --> 00:31:26,030
But there's no evidence

786
00:31:26,030 --> 00:31:26,720
that he did use any of them.

787
00:31:26,720 --> 00:31:28,920
But we can't rule out that he did either.

788
00:31:29,400 --> 00:31:30,750
Do you think there's a possibility

789
00:31:30,750 --> 00:31:32,350
of acquitting him

790
00:31:33,440 --> 00:31:34,170
in this case?

791
00:31:35,070 --> 00:31:35,830
Acquit him?

792
00:31:36,550 --> 00:31:38,550
A case with such huge public impact?

793
00:31:40,520 --> 00:31:41,040
I think

794
00:31:41,060 --> 00:31:42,510
he's likely to be the murderer.

795
00:31:42,510 --> 00:31:43,350
Likely?

796
00:31:44,360 --> 00:31:45,310
What we are discussing now

797
00:31:45,310 --> 00:31:46,410
is certainty!

798
00:31:46,580 --> 00:31:48,790
But there are still doubts.

799
00:31:49,160 --> 00:31:49,720
If...

800
00:31:50,070 --> 00:31:51,160
I'm just saying if.

801
00:31:52,350 --> 00:31:53,350
If we get it wrong,

802
00:31:53,880 --> 00:31:55,410
then we'll have no way back.

803
00:31:56,550 --> 00:31:58,280
I suggest we leave some leeway.

804
00:32:04,240 --> 00:32:05,570
Let's resume the trial.

805
00:32:06,550 --> 00:32:07,480
This court holds

806
00:32:07,960 --> 00:32:09,310
that the judgment of the first instance

807
00:32:09,310 --> 00:32:11,240
correctly established the facts,

808
00:32:11,680 --> 00:32:13,540
but the sentencing was improper.

809
00:32:13,640 --> 00:32:15,830
The court hereby
renders the following judgment:

810
00:32:15,830 --> 00:32:16,550
The criminal judgment

811
00:32:16,550 --> 00:32:18,590
of the Binjiang Intermediate People's Court

812
00:32:18,590 --> 00:32:20,640
for Case No. 239,

813
00:32:20,640 --> 00:32:21,900
is hereby overturned.

814
00:32:22,640 --> 00:32:24,310
The appellant, Qian Xingliang,

815
00:32:24,310 --> 00:32:26,240
convicted of intentional homicide,

816
00:32:26,240 --> 00:32:27,440
is sentenced to death

817
00:32:28,070 --> 00:32:29,440
with a 2-year reprieve

818
00:32:30,000 --> 00:32:32,400
and deprived of political rights for life.

819
00:32:32,680 --> 00:32:34,960
This judgment is final.

820
00:32:36,510 --> 00:32:38,040
The court is now adjourned.

821
00:32:41,920 --> 00:32:43,350
This is unfair!

822
00:32:44,290 --> 00:32:45,800
Judges!

823
00:32:45,830 --> 00:32:47,510
This is unfair!

824
00:32:48,000 --> 00:32:49,750
He killed...

825
00:32:49,830 --> 00:32:51,920
Judges!

826
00:32:52,310 --> 00:32:54,310
This is unfair!

827
00:33:00,640 --> 00:33:02,240
Let's go. Let's go. Let's go.

828
00:33:32,880 --> 00:33:33,440
Well,

829
00:33:33,440 --> 00:33:34,030
at least

830
00:33:34,050 --> 00:33:35,240
we saved a life, right?

831
00:33:35,240 --> 00:33:36,440
We can count this as a phased victory,

832
00:33:36,440 --> 00:33:36,880
right?

833
00:33:39,680 --> 00:33:40,240
Lu,

834
00:33:41,790 --> 00:33:43,120
you did great this time.

835
00:33:43,640 --> 00:33:46,840
You're ready to conduct
independent defense from now on.

836
00:33:47,680 --> 00:33:48,510
No way.

837
00:33:49,070 --> 00:33:50,310
I'll lose my footing without you.

838
00:33:50,310 --> 00:33:51,440
I need you by my side.

839
00:33:52,750 --> 00:33:53,550
I'm old.

840
00:33:57,960 --> 00:33:59,620
"Leniency in doubtful cases"

841
00:34:00,000 --> 00:34:02,880
and "innocence in doubtful cases"
only differ in one word.

842
00:34:02,880 --> 00:34:05,740
God knows how many years
it'll take to make the jump.

843
00:34:05,880 --> 00:34:06,680
I'm...

844
00:34:08,960 --> 00:34:09,760
I'm afraid...

845
00:34:13,030 --> 00:34:13,920
You're not old!

846
00:34:15,230 --> 00:34:15,480
Come on,

847
00:34:15,480 --> 00:34:17,080
how can you lose confidence?

848
00:34:17,639 --> 00:34:18,190
If you quit,

849
00:34:18,190 --> 00:34:19,449
then I'm quitting too!

850
00:34:19,520 --> 00:34:20,190
I just admire

851
00:34:20,190 --> 00:34:22,110
your spirit
of fighting on despite repeated setbacks!

852
00:34:22,110 --> 00:34:23,120
I went to law school

853
00:34:23,120 --> 00:34:24,000
because I saw you

854
00:34:24,000 --> 00:34:24,670
practicing law!

855
00:34:24,670 --> 00:34:25,880
That's why I wanted to become a lawyer!

856
00:34:25,880 --> 00:34:27,360
How can you say that?

857
00:34:31,320 --> 00:34:32,070
I'm really afraid

858
00:34:32,070 --> 00:34:33,600
I won't live to see that day.

859
00:34:34,370 --> 00:34:35,409
Why wouldn't you?

860
00:34:35,440 --> 00:34:36,500
I'll be right here with you!

861
00:34:36,500 --> 00:34:37,830
We'll see it together!

862
00:34:39,360 --> 00:34:40,320
What are you doing?

863
00:34:40,320 --> 00:34:40,880
Get up!

864
00:34:41,510 --> 00:34:42,150
Don't you call yourself

865
00:34:42,150 --> 00:34:43,320
a pessimistic optimist?

866
00:34:43,320 --> 00:34:44,719
Get up and be optimistic!

867
00:34:45,320 --> 00:34:46,880
Look at you. At your age,

868
00:34:47,350 --> 00:34:48,230
you barely make any money,

869
00:34:48,230 --> 00:34:50,360
and all you do is spout such bleak talk!

870
00:35:03,550 --> 00:35:04,280
Thank you.

871
00:35:06,930 --> 00:35:08,300
You're welcome.

872
00:35:10,110 --> 00:35:11,570
You're welcome? What for?

873
00:35:11,960 --> 00:35:12,840
Just mouth it.

874
00:35:13,230 --> 00:35:14,000
My duty.

875
00:35:18,150 --> 00:35:19,230
My duty.

876
00:35:38,630 --> 00:35:39,670
How have you and Meifang

877
00:35:39,670 --> 00:35:41,200
been getting along lately?

878
00:35:41,280 --> 00:35:41,960
Not bad.

879
00:35:45,150 --> 00:35:45,930
Xia,

880
00:35:46,370 --> 00:35:47,120
I understand

881
00:35:47,920 --> 00:35:50,030
you're upset about that case.

882
00:35:50,530 --> 00:35:51,280
But the Provincial High Court

883
00:35:51,280 --> 00:35:53,080
didn't send it back for retrial.

884
00:35:53,590 --> 00:35:54,920
What does that tell you?

885
00:35:55,280 --> 00:35:57,030
It means our work

886
00:35:57,230 --> 00:35:59,030
was solid.

887
00:36:00,510 --> 00:36:02,630
The second-instance verdict is final.

888
00:36:02,630 --> 00:36:03,710
The Qian Xingliang case

889
00:36:03,710 --> 00:36:04,440
ends here.

890
00:36:05,320 --> 00:36:06,550
He got to keep his life.

891
00:36:06,550 --> 00:36:08,150
That's already more
than he could have hoped for.

892
00:36:08,150 --> 00:36:09,350
Try not to dwell on it.

893
00:36:11,030 --> 00:36:13,230
The commutation to death with reprieve

894
00:36:13,520 --> 00:36:14,480
means the High Court

895
00:36:14,480 --> 00:36:15,550
also recognizes flaws

896
00:36:15,550 --> 00:36:16,950
in the evidence.

897
00:36:17,630 --> 00:36:19,960
They are leaving themselves some leeway.

898
00:36:19,960 --> 00:36:21,230
What else could they do?

899
00:36:21,230 --> 00:36:21,920
Acquit him?

900
00:36:25,670 --> 00:36:27,970
Who would dare make that judgment?

901
00:36:28,000 --> 00:36:28,800
I would dare!

902
00:36:30,760 --> 00:36:31,880
If I were the presiding judge
of the High Court,

903
00:36:31,880 --> 00:36:32,610
I would dare!

904
00:36:32,650 --> 00:36:33,760
I would acquit him!

905
00:36:36,000 --> 00:36:37,150
You're still young.

906
00:36:37,580 --> 00:36:39,430
I hope that when you reach my age,

907
00:36:39,920 --> 00:36:42,520
you still have that kind
of courage and spirit.

908
00:36:49,000 --> 00:36:49,730
Chief Judge,

909
00:36:54,800 --> 00:36:55,800
I want to resign.

910
00:37:00,800 --> 00:37:02,320
S-Say that again?

911
00:37:04,150 --> 00:37:06,750
I don't think
that with my ability and courage,

912
00:37:07,760 --> 00:37:09,250
I'm worthy of being a judge.

913
00:37:09,250 --> 00:37:10,020
Nonsense!

914
00:37:10,440 --> 00:37:12,230
You're just wallowing in self-pity,

915
00:37:12,230 --> 00:37:13,960
putting on a show for yourself,

916
00:37:14,030 --> 00:37:16,030
and throwing a tantrum to the court!

917
00:37:17,920 --> 00:37:18,480
True.

918
00:37:19,600 --> 00:37:21,360
This is the reality of judicature

919
00:37:21,360 --> 00:37:22,220
in our country.

920
00:37:22,870 --> 00:37:25,270
There's not much an individual can change!

921
00:37:25,510 --> 00:37:26,560
But if everyone

922
00:37:26,800 --> 00:37:27,640
backs off

923
00:37:27,670 --> 00:37:28,870
at the first setback,

924
00:37:29,110 --> 00:37:31,150
won't that make it even harder
to change anything?

925
00:37:31,150 --> 00:37:32,360
This is not courage.

926
00:37:32,840 --> 00:37:33,970
It's being a coward!

927
00:37:52,480 --> 00:37:53,110
Xia,

928
00:37:54,230 --> 00:37:55,710
we all have high expectations

929
00:37:55,710 --> 00:37:56,920
for you.

930
00:37:57,670 --> 00:37:59,550
To become a qualified judge,

931
00:38:00,000 --> 00:38:02,400
you still have countless trials ahead.

932
00:38:03,110 --> 00:38:05,040
You've barely begun your journey.

933
00:38:06,400 --> 00:38:08,130
You cannot imagine how arduous

934
00:38:08,440 --> 00:38:10,700
the work of many legal professionals is.

935
00:38:12,760 --> 00:38:13,440
I know.

936
00:38:13,760 --> 00:38:14,760
No, you don't.

937
00:38:16,000 --> 00:38:18,070
If you don't put yourself in their shoes,

938
00:38:18,070 --> 00:38:19,800
you won't be able to empathize.

939
00:38:24,480 --> 00:38:25,340
How about this?

940
00:38:25,440 --> 00:38:26,760
I'll give you some time off.

941
00:38:26,760 --> 00:38:27,820
When you come back,

942
00:38:28,110 --> 00:38:29,110
we'll talk again.

943
00:38:33,490 --> 00:38:34,820
Thank you, Chief Judge.

944
00:38:35,320 --> 00:38:36,190
For what?

945
00:38:37,190 --> 00:38:39,160
I've been saving up
all your unused family leave

946
00:38:39,160 --> 00:38:40,620
from the past three years.

947
00:38:41,280 --> 00:38:43,140
Although it's against the rules,

948
00:38:43,590 --> 00:38:44,720
I'll put in a request

949
00:38:45,320 --> 00:38:46,320
for an exception.

950
00:39:00,030 --> 00:39:00,490
Come on.

951
00:39:03,480 --> 00:39:04,110
Drink.

952
00:39:23,480 --> 00:39:24,670
Your case was a tragedy,

953
00:39:24,670 --> 00:39:25,600
so you resigned.

954
00:39:28,800 --> 00:39:29,800
Your case was also a tragedy,

955
00:39:29,800 --> 00:39:30,930
so you resigned too.

956
00:39:33,710 --> 00:39:35,070
I wouldn't call mine a comedy,

957
00:39:35,070 --> 00:39:36,920
but I didn't handle it well either.

958
00:39:36,920 --> 00:39:37,400
Right?

959
00:39:38,150 --> 00:39:39,080
How can I resign?

960
00:39:39,500 --> 00:39:40,360
I can't resign.

961
00:39:40,360 --> 00:39:41,030
My home is here.

962
00:39:41,030 --> 00:39:41,960
My family is here.

963
00:39:41,960 --> 00:39:42,610
How can I resign?

964
00:39:42,610 --> 00:39:43,590
I have no choice.

965
00:39:46,440 --> 00:39:47,590
There's plenty of gossip
circulating in the court these days.

966
00:39:47,590 --> 00:39:48,110
They say

967
00:39:48,840 --> 00:39:50,700
Yu Gaoyuan is all bark and no bite.

968
00:39:50,890 --> 00:39:51,600
They say

969
00:39:51,630 --> 00:39:52,400
what I did was just a slap on the wrist

970
00:39:52,400 --> 00:39:53,300
for Song Xiaoguang.

971
00:39:53,300 --> 00:39:55,760
They complain
that I only sentenced him to five years.

972
00:39:55,760 --> 00:39:56,940
They also say....

973
00:39:57,440 --> 00:39:58,190
I'm just after fame.

974
00:39:58,190 --> 00:39:59,020
Do I even have that kind of pull?

975
00:39:59,020 --> 00:39:59,880
I'm after fame?

976
00:40:00,370 --> 00:40:01,760
I wanted to give him
a death penalty with reprieve!

977
00:40:01,760 --> 00:40:02,460
Would Zhang Deshan have agreed?

978
00:40:02,460 --> 00:40:04,660
Would the court president have agreed?

979
00:40:13,880 --> 00:40:15,880
What are you two planning to do next?

980
00:40:17,510 --> 00:40:18,710
I want to go to Bieshan

981
00:40:20,800 --> 00:40:22,000
to see Lihui.

982
00:40:24,880 --> 00:40:26,880
Have you two been in touch recently?

983
00:40:28,760 --> 00:40:30,230
I just suddenly miss her.

984
00:40:31,230 --> 00:40:32,400
I want to see her

985
00:40:33,110 --> 00:40:34,190
and talk to her.

986
00:40:35,150 --> 00:40:35,840
I heard the conditions there

987
00:40:35,840 --> 00:40:37,110
are extremely harsh.

988
00:40:37,920 --> 00:40:39,980
It's almost like serving a sentence.

989
00:40:40,800 --> 00:40:42,000
I want to see

990
00:40:44,510 --> 00:40:45,800
how she endures it.

991
00:40:47,360 --> 00:40:48,070
Alright.

992
00:40:49,760 --> 00:40:50,960
I'll go with you then.

993
00:40:52,710 --> 00:40:53,110
Go.

994
00:40:53,800 --> 00:40:54,860
You should both go.

995
00:41:04,550 --> 00:41:05,920
Presiding Judge Yu.

996
00:41:09,280 --> 00:41:10,080
Good heavens.

997
00:41:11,310 --> 00:41:11,840
Mr. Qiao.

998
00:41:13,550 --> 00:41:15,010
Wait outside for a moment.

999
00:41:17,160 --> 00:41:18,150
I've been looking

1000
00:41:18,150 --> 00:41:19,590
for an opportunity to thank you.

1001
00:41:19,590 --> 00:41:20,070
Please, don't.

1002
00:41:20,070 --> 00:41:20,590
Really.

1003
00:41:21,440 --> 00:41:22,640
You handled this case

1004
00:41:24,230 --> 00:41:25,000
very well.

1005
00:41:25,400 --> 00:41:25,880
Really.

1006
00:41:26,230 --> 00:41:27,430
Exceptionally well.

1007
00:41:28,190 --> 00:41:29,320
It wasn't easy.

1008
00:41:29,800 --> 00:41:31,330
You've worked really hard.

1009
00:41:31,840 --> 00:41:32,920
Can I sit down

1010
00:41:33,280 --> 00:41:34,030
and toast you?

1011
00:41:34,030 --> 00:41:34,690
Please sit.

1012
00:41:48,320 --> 00:41:49,450
He's the ringleader

1013
00:41:49,760 --> 00:41:51,760
of such a big hooligan gang

1014
00:41:52,230 --> 00:41:54,030
and such a powerful princeling.

1015
00:41:54,710 --> 00:41:57,170
You actually managed
to put him behind bars.

1016
00:41:58,230 --> 00:41:58,920
Honestly,

1017
00:41:59,630 --> 00:42:01,150
it's an extraordinary feat.

1018
00:42:01,150 --> 00:42:02,410
You've worked so hard.

1019
00:42:04,150 --> 00:42:05,480
May I toast you?

1020
00:42:05,630 --> 00:42:06,090
Come on.

1021
00:42:13,920 --> 00:42:14,710
This one

1022
00:42:15,760 --> 00:42:16,820
is for my daughter.

1023
00:42:18,590 --> 00:42:19,190
Of course.

1024
00:42:23,690 --> 00:42:25,190
Do you still remember my daughter?

1025
00:42:25,190 --> 00:42:26,590
Of course I remember her.

1026
00:42:31,480 --> 00:42:32,110
My god,

1027
00:42:32,840 --> 00:42:33,960
this is good wine.

1028
00:42:34,760 --> 00:42:36,840
I spilled such good wine just now?

1029
00:42:38,110 --> 00:42:40,640
Did Song Xiaoguang's mother
give this to you?

1030
00:42:42,110 --> 00:42:42,960
Or his uncle?

1031
00:42:46,440 --> 00:42:48,280
My god, it just dawned on me.

1032
00:42:49,360 --> 00:42:50,960
You're celebrating, right?

1033
00:42:51,630 --> 00:42:52,440
Or are you discussing

1034
00:42:52,440 --> 00:42:53,670
what to do next?

1035
00:42:54,710 --> 00:42:56,030
If I'm not mistaken,

1036
00:42:56,710 --> 00:42:58,110
Song Xiaoguang should

1037
00:42:58,880 --> 00:43:00,480
be getting medical parole in a few days,
right?
